rces I  don't think he would have necessarily  had an easy time defeating Goldwater in  64 that's another reason he had to go to  Texas he knew he had lost the whole  south when I read these books they drive  me crazy there's a book by British  historian saying that Kennedys were you  know remiss on civil rights and they  didn't care about sell vegetables yes  they were slow on civil rights that's  clear they were very afraid of splitting  the Democratic Party of losing the  Democratic South and they did they did  finally do the right thing and that's  what happened they split the Democratic  Party something we still see today that  started with Jack Kennedy because he  finally stood up and he did the right  thing on civil rights and so he had to  go to Texas because that was along with  Florida probably the only states in the  deep south he could have won so the  country you know we all think of him as  this charming charismatic prince who  would have had an easy time being  reelected in 64 but the truth is he he  probably would have had a tough tough  campaign  and the fact that spas Reagan met Oswald  when he came back from the Soviet Union  and helped Oswald get back to Texas and  spas Reagan was a Nazi collaborator from  the Ukraine originally and why he would  help Oswald get back to Dallas is is a  mystery to me and it's also mr. me why  the CIA hired Reinhard Galen who was  Hitler's top Intel official on his  Eastern Front in the Soviet Union  right now you're down a tunnel that I I  wasn't able to go down but yeah I mean  the major point you're making is very  interesting one which is you know Oswald  defected to the Soviet Union and then  came back with with surprising ease  Senator Richard Schweiker from  Pennsylvania who on the church committee  looked into the Kennedy assassination  said it made a very famous statement the  time saying the fingerprints of  intelligence are all over Lee Harvey  Oswald and I believe that's true maybe  one more and then we